cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agnostic Framework: a unification hypothesis for intelligence and how ideas become canon"
message: "If you use or reference this framework, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - alias: "Pav"
    family-names: "Pav"
    given-names: "Pav"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/a70m123r/agnostic-framework"
url: "https://a70m123r.github.io/agnostic-framework/"
abstract: >-
  A unification hypothesis treating intelligence as a fuzzy-to-canon compiler.
  Observers (harness + wrapper + inner sandbox + action-space) encounter a fuzzy
  candidate field, generate plausible interpretations (A⁺), check candidates
  against constraints (A⁻), and admit what survives as canon. The compilation
  is asymmetric — A⁻ is the primary discipline. Canon propagates as
  carrier-artifacts and re-renders at receiving observers. Observers symbiose
  via slow-fast pushouts. Independently developed in the LeCun research lineage
  (world models, JEPA, energy-based reasoning) with multi-agent and
  multi-observer extensions.
keywords:
  - intelligence
  - multi-agent systems
  - energy-based models
  - observer-class theory
  - constraint satisfaction
  - canon formation
  - emergent garden
  - JEPA
  - world models
  - Lakatosian research programme
